# Value Mappings

Mappings are dictionaries that rename raw values to human-readable labels in widget columns.

## Definition

Define mappings at the dashboard top level:

```yaml
mappings:
  languages:
    entries:
      arabic: AR
      english: EN
      french: FR
      german: DE
      spanish: ES
      russian: RU
      unknown: ""
    fallback: original                  # Keep original value if no match

  media_sources:
    entries:
      Facebook_abakus: FB_A
      Facebook Ads: FB
      googleadwords_int: GA
      TikTok: TT
      True organic: Org
    # No fallback = unmapped values show as-is

  platforms:
    entries:
      ios: iOS
      android: Android
      web: Web
```

## Fallback behavior

```yaml
# Keep original value if not in entries
fallback: original

# Use a fixed default string
fallback:
  default: "Unknown"

# No fallback (omit field) = show original value as-is
```

## Usage in columns

Reference a mapping in rich_table or pivot column definitions:

```yaml
columns:
  - id: language
    label: Lang
    type: dimension
    mapping: { id: languages }           # Applies languages mapping

  - id: media_source
    label: MS
    type: dimension
    mapping: { id: media_sources }

  - id: payment_source
    label: Payment source
    type: dimension
    mapping: { id: platforms }
    # Can override fallback per column:
    # mapping: { id: platforms, fallback: { default: "Other" } }
```

## Usage in projection columns

Projection column metadata can also reference mappings:

```yaml
projections:
  daily_costs_by_source:
    sql: |
      SELECT media_source, SUM(costs) as costs
      FROM {{source:total_by_ad}}
      GROUP BY 1
    columns:
      media_source: { type: string, description: "Media source", mapping: media_sources }
```

## Column normalize

Independent of mappings, columns can normalize text casing:

```yaml
columns:
  - id: plan_name
    label: Type
    type: dimension
    normalize: capitalize               # capitalize | uppercase | lowercase
```

- `capitalize`: "max" -> "Max"
- `uppercase`: "max" -> "MAX"
- `lowercase`: "MAX" -> "max"

## Directory-based dashboards: shared mappings

In directory-based dashboards, mappings can be defined in `_shared/_mappings.yaml`:

```yaml
# _shared/_mappings.yaml — flat dict, merged into dashboard mappings
languages:
  entries:
    english: EN
    russian: RU
  fallback: original
```

Merge rule: dashboard `_shared/_mappings.yaml` is base; tab-level mappings (tab `_shared` or tab-content files) override on key conflict.

## Dashboard-level shared mappings

A dashboard can define shared mappings in `_shared/_mappings.yaml` (next to `+layout.yaml`). These are inherited by **all tabs** in that dashboard:

```yaml
# dashboards/<root>/<dashboard>/_shared/_mappings.yaml — inherited by all tabs
languages:
  entries:
    english: EN
    russian: RU
  fallback: original
```

Merge rule: dashboard = base, tab mappings override on key conflict (same as tab-level `_shared/`).

## Rules

- Mapping keys are case-sensitive. The raw value must match exactly.
- Mappings are applied at render time, not in SQL.
- Use `fallback: original` to pass through unmapped values unchanged.
- Mappings are defined once at dashboard level and reused across all widgets.
- For column-specific overrides, set `fallback` in the column's `mapping` ref.
